% Obligation: ~(x & y) == (~x) | (~y), for every pair of 64-bit words.
% The rewrite every peephole pass wants to make. It is also the cheapest
% obligation in the corpus that exercises THREE different gate definitions
% (bb_and, bb_or, bb_not) against each other in one claim: bb_not is pure literal
% negation and emits no clauses at all, so a sign error there is invisible to any
% test that only ever negates twice.
obligation de_morgan_and
1 var x
2 var y
3 and 1 2
4 not 3
5 not 1
6 not 2
7 or 5 6
8 eq 4 7
prove 8
